'''Horizon Base''' was an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] shipping [[Spaceport|port]] and [[Fuel|refueling]] station located on a [[Unidentified planet (Horizon Base)|planet]] in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. In [[3 BBY]], during the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Spectres|members]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] group [[Phoenix Cell]] performed a [[heist at Horizon Base|heist]] the station, acquiring fuel for their [[fleet]]. Later, during the [[First Order-Resistance War]], [[First Order]] forces engaged in a [[Battle for Horizon Base|battle]] at Horizon Base.

==Description==
[[File:Horizon_Base_planet.jpg|thumb|left|220px|Horizon Base was located on a planet in the Outer Rim.]]
Horizon Base was an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] outpost that was both a shipping [[Spaceport|port]] and [[Fuel|refueling]] station.<ref name="Helmet Collection 24">{{HelmetCollectionCite|24|Databank A-Z}}</ref> It was located on a a [[Unidentified planet (Horizon Base)|planet]]<ref name="Concept Art Gallery" /> in [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="Helmet Collection 24" /> in a [[sector]] that was controlled by the Empire<ref name="TFD" /> by [[3 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> The base rose out of portal-like underground installations. In total, six docking areas were present, with the circular buildings surrounded by dozens of individual docking bays&mdash;three of which directly surrounded the main spire, while the other two were more distantly adjacent. The main spire of the base also rose slightly higher then the other docking areas. The exterior of the base included cargo containers, barrels, and a market. Civilians were present on the station and would sell items such as [[droid]] parts.<ref name="TFD" /> The interior of the station included corridors as well as cargo loading areas.<ref name="Battle for Horizon Base" />

==History==
{{Quote|All right. After we grab the fuel, we'll have to blast our way out of here fast. Chopper, be ready.|Kanan Jarrus gives final instructions to Chopper as the rebels prepare to steal fuel from Horizon Base|<ref name="TFD" />}}
[[File:HorizonBaseMission.jpg|thumb|right|260px|Finn and Gannis Ducain on Horizon Base]]
In 3 BBY,<ref name="Timelines" /> during the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the Empire and the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], the rebel group known as the [[Spectres]], including [[Hera Syndulla]], [[Kanan Jarrus]], [[Sabine Wren]], [[Garazeb Orrelios]], and [[Ezra Bridger]], [[Heist at Horizon Base|raided]] Horizon Base to steal [[fuel]] needed for [[Phoenix Cell]]'s [[fleet]]. During the mission, the rebel [[astromech droid]] [[C1-10P|Chopper]], who had been left to guard the [[Ghost|ship]], was accidentally left behind after the others left with the stolen fuel. Stranded, the [[droid]] chose to board the [[class four container transport]] designated [[Imperial Cargo Transport 241|241]] that was departing the station and, with the help of a new ally, the [[inventory droid]] [[AP-5]], soon reunited with Phoenix Cell.<ref name="TFD" />

By [[34 ABY]]<ref name="Date">"[[The Battle for Horizon Base]]" takes place between the events of {{Film|VIII}} and {{Film|IX}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]] and [[35 ABY]] respectively. Therefore, "The Battle for Horizon Base" must take place between 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]] and 35 ABY.</ref> Horizon Base was controlled by the [[First Order]]. During the [[First Order-Resistance War]], [[Resistance]] members [[Poe Dameron]], [[Finn]], and [[Gannis Ducain]] traveled to Horizon Base on a [[Battle for Horizon Base|mission]] to recruit [[Mezlo]]'s [[Oruan]] group for the Resistance. As Finn and Ducain infiltrated the base, they were spotted by two [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] who they defeated by dropping cargo crates on them before running away. Navigating through the inside the base, the two agents were caught by a [[candori]], and met Mezlo's group of refugees. They were interrupted by several more stormtroopers, but fought them off and attempted unsuccessfully to recruit the Oruans, as they preferred to find their place elsewhere. However, the Oruans did agree to help the Resistance in a time of need.<ref name="Battle for Horizon Base" />

==Behind the scenes==
Horizon Base first appeared in "[[The Forgotten Droid]]," the nineteenth episode of the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Two|second season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="TFD" />The episode premiered on [[March 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/the-forgotten-droid-episode-guide|text="The Forgotten Droid" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref>

